        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\cot x$.",
          "worked": "Using the complementary-angle identities, where defined:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}-x\\right)&=\\frac{\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}-x\\right)}{\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}-x\\right)}\\\\\\tan\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}-x\\right)&=\\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x}\\\\\\tan\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}-x\\right)&=\\cot x.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
